{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "nodeID": "155",
   "text": "Why do global trade imbalances persist, and why could they worsen before improving?",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "question",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#Q"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "156",
   "text": "If large economies save externally, another economy must absorb the surplus",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#P1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "157",
   "text": "Weak domestic demand tends to reduce imports and raise surpluses",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#P2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "158",
   "text": "Saving above domestic investment pushes capital and demand abroad",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#P3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "159",
   "text": "Together they roughly mirror the U.S. manufacturing deficit",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#D1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "160",
   "text": "Germany and other surplus economies run restrictive demand policies",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#D2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "161",
   "text": "Korea, Taiwan, Singapore, and Thailand remain export oriented",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#D3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "162",
   "text": "Current account ~$200–250B with augmented deficit near 12% of GDP",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#D4"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "163",
   "text": "East Asian aggregate saving remains close to 40%",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#D5"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "164",
   "text": "Modest stimulus failed to offset tightening and the trade war",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#D6"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "165",
   "text": "Large relative to the country's limited export base",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#D7"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "166",
   "text": "Lower imports and excess saving generate European surpluses",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#M1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "167",
   "text": "China saves more than its economy can sustainably absorb",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#M2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "168",
   "text": "Less domestic absorption pushes the external balance upward",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#M3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "169",
   "text": "North America takes the other side through external deficits and debt",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#M4"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "170",
   "text": "Looser fiscal policy could directly raise domestic absorption",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#C1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "171",
   "text": "China's underlying problem is exceptionally high saving",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#C2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "172",
   "text": "Large public investment prevents an even larger external surplus",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#C3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "173",
   "text": "Its external debt stock is already large relative to exports",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#C4"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "174",
   "text": "Europe still lacks demand and China's excess-saving problem remains; the U.S. cannot indefinitely absorb the resulting surpluses",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "main_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#K"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "175",
   "text": "Tighter U.S. fiscal policy would also reduce the American trade deficit",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "other_explanation",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#X"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "176",
   "text": "Japan runs a surplus despite relatively loose fiscal policy",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "counterpoint",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#R1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "177",
   "text": "The current flow deficit is not obviously unsustainable today",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#QF1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "178",
   "text": "Fiscal and credit stimulus currently absorbs much of China's excess saving",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_sep_20_19#QF2"
  },
